      "at": "2026-10-05T20:06:58Z",
      "excerpt": "Valid. Fixed in 33e11e6 on the filter side: `examples.yml` lists `examples/playground/**` again after `!**/*.md`, with a comment that the content hash covers the playground's Markdown. So a README edit there still runs `hash_examples.py --check`. I didn't change `hashed_files()`, because that changes what the macro benchmark baselines key on, which is beyond what this PR is for. --- _Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_"
    },
    {
      "by": "masenf",
      "association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "at": "2026-10-05T20:07:00Z",
      "excerpt": "Added in 33e11e6 (`test_action_evaluates_each_event`), along with the same coverage described on the Greptile thread above. --- _Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_"
    },
    {
      "by": "masenf",
      "association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "at": "2026-10-05T20:07:02Z",
      "excerpt": "Keeping this as it is. Every local action in the repo uses `action.yml`, and the existing `test_action_descriptions_carry_no_expressions` in the same file also only globs `*/action.yml`, so that naming is already the convention the tests rely on. If someone later adds an `action.yaml`, it's the same one-line widening in both tests. --- _Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_"
    },
    {
      "by": "masenf",
      "association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "at": "2026-10-05T20:07:04Z",
      "excerpt": "Agreed, done in 33e11e6. The unit-tests filter now negates `.github/workflows/**`, `.github/actions/**` and `.github/rulesets/**`, replacing its own-file negations, with a comment that `test_workflow_gates.py` is why. The evaluator fixture copies that list, with cases for another workflow, both actions and the ruleset. --- _Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_"
    },
    {
      "by": "masenf",
      "association": "COLLABORATOR",
      "at": "2026-10-05T20:07:05Z",
      "excerpt": "Done in 33e11e6. The paragraph is re-wrapped at 80, and the sentence now says the jobs skip on the pull requests and pushes the filter leaves out, and that one workflow's jobs can filter differently. --- _Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_"
    },
    {
      "by": "greptile-apps",
      "association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "at": "2026-10-05T20:07:24Z",
      "excerpt": "That’s a fair distinction. The `python3` calls are intentionally part of the action’s runner-side implementation, not contributor commands in the project environment; the script is stdlib-only, and the existing pull-request branch already uses the same invocation. The comment also documents why installing `uv` is intentionally avoided. I’m withdrawing this finding."
